From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:17:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 136/147] hjviewer: the support codes' wire as hjv-api speaks
 it (1.9)

- A support code's pc-code result says "staff": whether hjv-api's answer
  brought a support grant this PC holds (the doc 3-7 check). Without
  `staff`, or with one this PC refuses, the PC shows P2's toast instead of
  P6, which promises a shield.
- A 401 from the waiting room (S-02's check, or the waiting thread) ends
  the login through hjv-access-login-ended, also when none of its codes is
  still open.
- The support link is the page's own address, with the trailing '/'
  (S10; no 307 on the first open).
- A used code's until_in above 7200 keeps the support PC for 2 hours
  instead of reading as over.
- S10, S11 (English) and P6 use 5-3's words, as hjv-api's SL6 does.
